From 8553cd0ed8ceadf51f5b04e4e0eef3bced7f7dd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo Suoranta <tksuoran@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:18:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] MSL: Inline precise arithmetic helpers on MSL 3.2

NoContraction (precise) add, sub and mul are emitted as calls to helpers
declared [[clang::optnone]], so the Metal compiler cannot inline them and
every precise operation becomes a real function call. In a fragment shader
with precise operations inside a loop (a shadow lookup per light) this costs
several times the whole shader: on an Apple M4 Pro the forward pass of a
43-light scene took 26.6 ms with the optnone helpers and 6.0 ms with them
inlined, with bit-identical output.

From MSL 3.2 the helpers are regular functions whose bodies start with
#pragma metal fp math_mode(safe) and #pragma metal fp contract(off). The
scoped pragmas keep every operation in the helper exact without preventing
inlining. Earlier MSL versions keep the optnone helpers.

(cherry picked from KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Cross commit
98cbb7c02be35364ecacc23dc0c038d2360b0ed0 onto e52532a6, the revision
MoltenVK pins. The conflicts were in context lines only: the pinned helper
bodies (fma(T(1), l, r) and the others) differ from upstream's, and are kept.)
